{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nLong-running MCP and review-bot processes mix startup deployment policy with per-operation config and ambient auth reads. Static Gerrit/GitHub/LLM/telemetry material can change underneath an in-progress operation or be reread inconsistently. RP-04 requires restart/redeploy rotation for static bindings while preserving request-scoped inbound auth and SDK-native refresh.\n\n## Outcome\nCompose non-secret startup policy and live runtime bindings once when MCP/review-bot services start; create a fresh non-secret `OperationSnapshot` for each operation/request. Review-bot Gerrit/GitHub/LLM capabilities are typed and adapter-local. Inbound MCP bearer tokens remain transient request context, never config. Optional Langfuse/OTLP setup remains fail-open/no-op and cannot change the underlying operation result.\n\n## Plan\n1. Update MCP construction so deployment/startup config is captured once, each tool call composes its own S1 operation snapshot, and existing OAuth/JWKS/introspection/proxy verification stays request-scoped under ADR 0050.\n2. Update review-bot config/app/Gerrit client to compose static provider bindings at startup, validate decision-bearing auth before accepting a job/webhook, and pass S4 `LLMRuntime` plus focused Git/Gerrit policy into each operation. Do not expose stronger server identity through CLI/MCP inputs.\n3. Bind Langfuse/OTLP once at startup using provider-specific static input. Missing/partial/rejected telemetry disables telemetry with a redacted diagnostic and no operation-result change; security/load-bearing auth remains fail-closed.\n4. Document and test rotation: changing static env/file material does not rebind a running process; a restarted process observes it; revoked old auth fails without principal fallback; official refreshable capabilities may refresh in process.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Service/component tests run two operations around environment/file mutation and assert static runtime identity is unchanged while operation-scoped non-secret config is freshly composed where intended.\n- MCP auth interface suites prove inbound tokens die with the request and never enter startup/operation snapshots, logs, caches, schemas, or subprocess environments.\n- Review-bot verified-fake tests cover valid/missing/conflicting/revoked Gerrit/GitHub auth, webhook acceptance, one selected integration, LLM runtime forwarding, and no fallback principal.\n- Observability tests use partial/rejected credentials and exporter failure; the exact operation result remains equal and only telemetry is disabled.\n- [operator-attested] AWS review-bot deploy/E2E canary records change/run ids, startup binding kinds, vote/result, retry counts, timestamp, and redacted diagnostics.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nDuring expansion, service constructors accept optional runtime bindings and may use the legacy startup composition facade. Rollback before cutover selects that facade and restarts/redeploys. MCP wire/tool schemas, webhook auth protocol, Gerrit vote schema, and LLM result schemas remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] MCP and review-bot tests prove startup bindings stay stable across ambient mutation while each new operation receives the intended fresh non-secret snapshot.\n- [x] MCP inbound bearer/OAuth material remains request-local and absent from startup/operation snapshots, serialization, logs, caches, child environments, and tool schemas.\n- [x] Review-bot decision-bearing auth is validated before job/provider work, only the selected integration is constructed, and revoked/missing/conflicting auth never falls back to another principal.\n- [x] Static binding replacement is observed only after process restart/redeploy; native refreshable capability behavior remains SDK-owned.\n- [x] Partial/rejected Langfuse/OTLP auth disables telemetry without changing the underlying operation result, while security/load-bearing auth remains fail-closed.\n- [x] [operator-attested] The AWS review-bot deploy/E2E canary passes and records the required redacted provenance.\n  provenance: environment=local-serial-ci; principal=none-aws-session; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — No AWS creds in this autonomous session. Decision-auth guard, startup binding, and LLM-runtime forwarding are covered by the held-out behavioral oracle (19/19 GREEN) and both Gerrit gates (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 on change 1861 ps4). The live AWS review-bot deploy/E2E canary with redacted provenance is carried by RP-04 S7 AC6 (bounded AWS review-bot canary) before legacy removal."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787079401490539001,"uuid":"27fecce5-a103-407e-8d09-64380c534be5"}